{"id": "swebq0058", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1244407635, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "where did starbucks get their logo?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0058.wav", "input_sha256": "97984d2503e6a23dfeb1602d9f186b96a771ac4d7648068523b6f98056da8777", "input_samples": 34162, "input_s": 2.135, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.7616, "act": 0.9993, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Starbucks got its logo from a twin-tailed mermaid, or siren, inspired by old nautical imagery. The founders wanted a seafaring theme because Starbucks began in Seattle, a port city, and its name was inspired by Starbuck, a character in Moby-Dick. While looking through old marine books, they found an image of a 16th-century Norse-style woodcut of a two-tailed siren, which became the basis for the Starbucks logo.", "expert_answer": "Starbucks got its logo from a **twin-tailed mermaid, or siren**, inspired by old nautical imagery.\n\nThe founders wanted a seafaring theme because Starbucks began in Seattle, a port city, and its name was inspired by **Starbuck**, a character in *Moby-Dick*. While looking through old marine books, they found an image of a **16th-century Norse-style woodcut of a two-tailed siren**, which became the basis for the Starbucks logo.", "transcript": "Where did Starbucks get their logo?\n", "asr_s": 0.5, "expert_s": 3.76, "expert_input_samples": 34162, "expert_input_s": 2.135, "expert_input_sha256": "97984d2503e6a23dfeb1602d9f186b96a771ac4d7648068523b6f98056da8777", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.233, "relay_synth_ms": 11116, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0058_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "206ef19b5b23076a62ec9e8c15c5199ef066d570cc096eb9932b3ef76635850f", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 25.4}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0058_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "bb13cdc05ce06a405d5e0158e30ca2cf7d610e3baa2a4674068f5f113dead3a3", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0058_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "873351993d2f7ae10e78e6626c48f97f5a82a08f1435ed755083a6bb238fd179", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.06, 1.106, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.054, 2.098, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.135, 2.191, 2.236, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.135, 3.189, 3.682, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.135, 4.198, 4.713, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.135, "last_real_feed_done": 2.191, "onset": 3.682, "gate_read_done": 3.683, "fire": 3.683, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.682, "stall_note": 3.683, "stall_first_pcm": 4.136, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.713, "expert_req": 3.683, "expert_resp": 7.945, "relay_synth_start": 7.946, "relay_first_pcm": 8.515, "relay_synth_end": 19.062, "first_any_pcm": 3.682, "first_answer_pcm": 8.515, "session_end": 19.375}, "ttfa_answer_s": 6.38, "ttfa_any_s": 1.547}
{"id": "swebq0069", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 369509382, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "what led to stalin rise in power?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0069.wav", "input_sha256": "9c9d1bd1d6699469011b26fa32cfe99e82f98ea206b2a6b14cd906ac2ed335c2", "input_samples": 37134, "input_s": 2.321, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.5761, "act": 0.9978, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Stalin’s rise to power was caused by a combination of political skill, control of the Communist Party bureaucracy, and the weakness/division of his rivals. In short, Stalin rose to power because he controlled the party machine, manipulated alliances, eliminated rivals politically, and took advantage of the uncertainty after Lenin’s death.", "expert_answer": "Stalin’s rise to power was caused by a combination of **political skill, control of the Communist Party bureaucracy, and the weakness/division of his rivals**.\n\nKey factors:\n\n1. **Lenin’s death in 1924**\n   - After Lenin died, there was no clear successor, creating a power struggle within the Soviet leadership.\n\n2. **Stalin’s position as General Secretary**\n   - As General Secretary of the Communist Party, Stalin controlled party appointments and promotions.\n   - He used this role to place loyal supporters in important positions.\n\n3. **Outmaneuvering rivals**\n   - Stalin formed temporary alliances to isolate opponents like **Leon Trotsky**, **Zinoviev**, **Kamenev**, and **Bukharin**.\n   - He defeated them one by one rather than confronting them all at once.\n\n4. **Trotsky’s weaknesses**\n   - Trotsky was brilliant and popular in the Red Army, but he was seen by many party members as arrogant and less politically practical.\n   - He also underestimated Stalin.\n\n5. **Stalin’s image as a loyal Leninist**\n   - Stalin presented himself as Lenin’s true heir, even though Lenin had warned against Stalin in his “Testament.”\n\n6. **Party discipline and bureaucracy**\n   - The Communist Party had become highly centralized.\n   - Stalin used this system to silence opposition and strengthen his control.\n\n7. **Policy appeal**\n   - Stalin’s idea of **“Socialism in One Country”** appealed to many Soviet officials because it seemed more practical than Trotsky’s call for worldwide revolution.\n\nIn short, **Stalin rose to power because he controlled the party machine, manipulated alliances, eliminated rivals politically, and took advantage of the uncertainty after Lenin’s death**.", "transcript": "What led to Stalin rise in power?\n", "asr_s": 0.36, "expert_s": 7.28, "expert_input_samples": 37134, "expert_input_s": 2.321, "expert_input_sha256": "9c9d1bd1d6699469011b26fa32cfe99e82f98ea206b2a6b14cd906ac2ed335c2", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 6.785, "relay_synth_ms": 8450, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0069_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "ae8499ce1ad9207d8e6aa72ef8db7d5a714f50050a4f400b6e808ddf16724249", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 20.84}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0069_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "63f7c0987fa30103204f9aa9cbaf9b76ca8e0c490aedfc6b2231e621d1fe3e65", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0069_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "c450300dd56e5ae3ec9ec4b60b91e1ecc65dd006b9dc4bca642484485875bd81", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.52}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.05, 1.09, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.053, 2.092, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.321, 2.373, 2.413, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.321, 3.376, 3.826, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.321, 4.375, 4.684, 0, 12480, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.321, "last_real_feed_done": 2.373, "onset": 3.826, "gate_read_done": 3.826, "fire": 3.826, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.826, "stall_note": 3.827, "stall_first_pcm": 4.268, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.684, "expert_req": 3.827, "expert_resp": 11.469, "relay_synth_start": 11.47, "relay_first_pcm": 12.051, "relay_synth_end": 19.92, "first_any_pcm": 3.826, "first_answer_pcm": 12.051, "session_end": 20.063}, "ttfa_answer_s": 9.73, "ttfa_any_s": 1.505}
{"id": "swebq0078", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2014987729, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "what colleges did albert einstein teach at?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0078.wav", "input_sha256": "43c1ce74569857f3048e9e2708a2227d86700ca11c94c65ab8c3bb0552d14211", "input_samples": 39363, "input_s": 2.46, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.581, "act": 0.9991, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Albert Einstein taught or held teaching/professorial posts at several institutions, including: University of Bern — lecturer/Privatdozent , University of Zurich — associate professor , Charles University in Prague — professor , ETH Zurich — professor , University of Berlin — professor/director role with limited teaching duties , Institute for Advanced Study, Princeton — professor/research faculty, though not a traditional college teaching post He is often associated with Princeton, but he was at the Institute for Advanced Study, not Princeton University itself.", "expert_answer": "Albert Einstein taught or held teaching/professorial posts at several institutions, including:\n\n- **University of Bern** — lecturer/Privatdozent\n- **University of Zurich** — associate professor\n- **Charles University in Prague** — professor\n- **ETH Zurich** — professor\n- **University of Berlin** — professor/director role with limited teaching duties\n- **Institute for Advanced Study, Princeton** — professor/research faculty, though not a traditional college teaching post\n\nHe is often associated with **Princeton**, but he was at the **Institute for Advanced Study**, not Princeton University itself.", "transcript": "What colleges did Albert Einstein teach at?\n", "asr_s": 0.41, "expert_s": 4.79, "expert_input_samples": 39363, "expert_input_s": 2.46, "expert_input_sha256": "43c1ce74569857f3048e9e2708a2227d86700ca11c94c65ab8c3bb0552d14211", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 2.572, "relay_synth_ms": 15839, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 2, "feed_lag_max_ms": 520, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 911, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0078_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "d9eef41a9a7c46edc8f99b30241a56e7d1be1633afb2457b4a07219a7b6a3f3c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 38.56}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0078_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "65ebda7e19440d65400a3e11cea883447e12558752d5e472be35ad748f681802", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0078_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "91f2616390108b07ebeb2198aba36ae50cc38866160e7fc0c156ac6e9545ff66", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 3.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.055, 1.098, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.054, 2.1, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.46, 2.513, 2.555, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.46, 3.517, 4.078, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.46, 5.035, 5.852, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.46, 5.909, 6.707, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.46, "last_real_feed_done": 2.513, "onset": 4.078, "gate_read_done": 4.078, "fire": 4.078, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.078, "stall_note": 4.079, "stall_first_pcm": 4.981, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 6.707, "expert_req": 4.078, "expert_resp": 9.279, "relay_synth_start": 9.28, "relay_first_pcm": 9.9, "relay_synth_end": 25.119, "first_any_pcm": 4.078, "first_answer_pcm": 9.9, "session_end": 25.773}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.44, "ttfa_any_s": 1.617}
